Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.32,0:00:03.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}How is the wind learned?\NWith a simple trick.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.55,0:00:09.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Keep one coordinate of each point, and\Nlay the transport clock out to the right.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.30,0:00:12.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Pair each noise point\Nwith a random snapshot;
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.40,0:00:14.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}join them with a straight string.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.97,0:00:18.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Thousands of strings, crossing everywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.89,0:00:20.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Pick one place, at one moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.80,0:00:24.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Several strings pass through,\Npointing different ways.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.24,0:00:27.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The network learns one arrow\Nthere: their {\c&HF09CB4&}average direction{\c&HF7F4F2&}.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.06,0:00:30.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}That is the whole training:\Nplain regression,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.79,0:00:33.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}like fitting a curve through points.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.17,0:00:37.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Follow the averaged wind, not the strings.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.16,0:00:41.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The paths bend, and drawn against\Nthe clock, they never cross.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.58,0:00:46.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Learn the average exactly, and the\Nnoise lands exactly on the data's crowd.
